Add attention-data-parallel awareness to the SGLang model gateway, applied as a
cherry-pick of commit a9c97c9f69 ("[Feature] Add --attn-dp-size and deprecate
--enable-dp-attention (#41818)") onto sgl-project/sglang gateway-v0.3.1.

CONTEXT: without dp-awareness the gateway's worker registration treats an
attention-data-parallel engine as one worker per group: the discover step reads the
engine's ServerInfo without the attention-DP size, so the per-rank
CreateLocalWorkerStep fan-out never happens and a subordinate member's registration
wedges in discover_metadata. Measured on this program's SGLang External DP shape as
ISSUE-5: the gateway holds one healthy worker where the documented contract is one
endpoint PER MEMBER, Router-balanced. The commit teaches ServerInfo the attn_dp_size,
adds num_dp_ranks(), and fans the local worker step out per rank under the new
--dp-aware flag.

AGAINST: sgl-project/sglang gateway-v0.3.1.

WHEN TO REMOVE: the first upstream gateway tag that carries a9c97c9f69 — bump
SGLANG_GATEWAY_VERSION to that tag and delete this patch.

TWO LINES MORE THAN THE CHERRY-PICK, AND WHY. gateway-v0.3.1's discover_metadata MOVES
model_path and served_model_name out of the server info it holds, because Option::filter takes
its receiver by value. Upstream's own commit rewrote that whole region to borrow through as_ref
and to read the identity from /model_info, so upstream's tree never partially moves the struct
and its borrow of the whole struct for num_dp_ranks is legal. The cherry-pick keeps
gateway-v0.3.1's moving block and adds a borrow of the whole struct, and a partial move forbids
that: the gateway crate does not compile, with error[E0382], borrow of partially moved value
server_info. Here the two moves become borrows, which is the compiler's own first suggestion, so
the whole-struct borrow is legal. Both lines matter: the borrow checker reports one error at a
time, so fixing only the served_model_name move produces the same error again on the next build.

THE DIFF BELOW IS REBASED ONTO gateway-v0.3.1's OWN LINE NUMBERING. The cherry-pick's hunks were
written against upstream's tree, whose identity region is longer, so their headers name lines that
gateway-v0.3.1 does not have. The content is the same change; the headers are this file's own.

Operator side: the SGLang External DP shape renders --dp-aware for this gateway
(pkg/worker/kvcache/router/argv.go).

